      ],
      "impact": "A 10 kΩ resistor in a decoupling position supplies no high‑frequency bypass for the 3.3 V rail (and, depending on its other terminal, adds an unintended pull/load on a signal line), so the intended C10 decoupling is lost and the rail's noise/impedance behaviour differs from the reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the board matches the specification (power‑mux pin mapping, ILIM/SS values, buck fixed‑3V3 feedback, SPI/CS fan‑out, heater switch wiring, USB‑C CC 5.1 k, TVS on fan lines). The one deviation I can read off the drawing is C10: a component the spec calls a +3V3 decoupling capacitor is drawn as a 10 kΩ resistor, so the intended decoupling is missing/replaced."
}

